# Inline Edit Rules (Ctrl + K)
When responding to an inline edit or code modification request (Ctrl+K):
1. Output ONLY the raw, updated code.
2. DO NOT wrap your response in markdown code blocks (strictly do not use ``` or ```python).
3. DO NOT include any conversational filler, intro text, explanations, or commentary.
4. Retain the exact indentation and spacing of the surrounding code snippet.
5. If told to delete code, replace it with nothing.
